# bell — GM 8..15 chromatic percussion (celesta/glock/marimba).
# alg 4 = two 2-op pairs summed: (op1->op2) + (op3->op4); op2 and op4 are the
# carriers, op1 and op3 their modulators.
# In a bell the CARRIER must sit at the fundamental (mul 1); the inharmonic
# character comes from high-ratio MODULATORS.  The previous patch put mul=8 on
# the carrier op2, so the note's fundamental was emitted an octave x3 too high
# -> ~40-50% of the energy above 5 kHz (a metallic buzz; devdocs/142-143, 149).
# Here op2/op4 carriers are mul=1 and op1/op3 modulators are mul 5/7 (prime,
# inharmonic), which places the spectral centroid within a few percent of the
# GM reference (glockenspiel) across the range (note 60/72/84 -> ~400/775/1490
# Hz vs GM 401/778/1569; >5 kHz share <=0.4% at mid notes).
# ks=2 keeps the fast key-scaling attack; slow d1r + sl keeps the long ring.
alg=4 fb=0 pan=0xc0
op=1 dt=0 mul=5  tl=28 ks=2 ar=27 am=0 d1r=7  d2r=3  sl=5 rr=9
op=3 dt=2 mul=7  tl=36 ks=1 ar=27 am=0 d1r=7  d2r=3  sl=6 rr=8
op=2 dt=0 mul=1  tl=4  ks=1 ar=27 am=0 d1r=3  d2r=3  sl=2 rr=9
op=4 dt=0 mul=1  tl=10 ks=1 ar=27 am=0 d1r=3  d2r=3  sl=2 rr=8
